    {
      "text": "Figure 3: Scalability of LLaDA. We evaluate the performance of LLaDA and our ARM baselines",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        256.42779541015625,
        504.0011901855469,
        265.45391845703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "trained on the same data across increasing pre-training computational FLOPs. LLaDA exhibits strong",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        267.45635986328125,
        504.0014953613281,
        276.3629150390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "scalability, matching the overall performance of ARMs on six tasks.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        278.3653564453125,
        379.052490234375,
        287.27191162109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3.1",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        311.8457946777344,
        120.4532470703125,
        320.80218505859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Scalability of LLaDA on Language Tasks",
      "bbox": [
        130.4158477783203,
        311.8457946777344,
        304.9107360839844,
        320.80218505859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We first investigate the scalability of LLaDA on downstream tasks in comparison with the ARM",
      "bbox": [
        107.53199768066406,
        334.0513610839844,
        503.9967041015625,
        342.9579162597656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "baselines we constructed. Specifically, at the 1B scale, we ensured that LLaDA and ARM shared",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        344.9603576660156,
        503.99749755859375,
        353.8669128417969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the same architecture, data, and all other configurations. At larger scales, we also report results",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        355.8693542480469,
        503.9974670410156,
        364.7759094238281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for LLaDA and ARM models of slightly different sizes trained on the same data due to resource",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        366.7783508300781,
        503.99737548828125,
        375.6849060058594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "limitations. Please refer to Appendix B.2 for more details. We use the pre-training computational",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        377.6873474121094,
        503.9974365234375,
        386.5939025878906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "cost as a unified scaling metric. For evaluation, we focused on six standard and diverse tasks.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        388.59637451171875,
        478.8777160644531,
        397.5029296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fig. 3 shows that LLaDA demonstrates impressive scalability, with its overall trend highly competitive",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        404.9853515625,
        504.00140380859375,
        413.89190673828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "with ARMs. Notably, on tasks such as MMLU and GSM8K, LLaDA exhibits even stronger scalability.",
      "bbox": [
        107.64099884033203,
        415.89434814453125,
        505.74163818359375,
        424.8009033203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Even on relatively weaker tasks like PIQA, the performance gap with ARMs narrows as scale increases.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        426.8033752441406,
        505.73944091796875,
        435.7099304199219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To account for the influence of outliers, we opted not to fit quantitative curves, avoiding potential",
      "bbox": [
        107.69100189208984,
        437.7123718261719,
        504.0033874511719,
        446.6189270019531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "misinterpretation. Nevertheless, the results clearly demonstrate the scalability of LLaDA.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        448.6213684082031,
        463.625,
        457.5279235839844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Considering LLaDA’s advantages on certain benchmarks, we hypothesize that this performance gain",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        465.0103759765625,
        503.9983825683594,
        473.91693115234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "stems from a key architectural difference: while autoregressive models optimize only left-to-right",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        475.91937255859375,
        503.997314453125,
        484.825927734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "conditional probabilities, LLaDA is trained to consider multiple conditioning directions, as detailed in",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        486.828369140625,
        504.0015563964844,
        495.73492431640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Appendix A.2, which may offer greater flexibility and lead to better generalization. This hypothesis is",
      "bbox": [
        107.64099884033203,
        497.73736572265625,
        504.00360107421875,
        506.6439208984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "motivated by LLaDA’s strong performance on reversal reasoning in Sec. 3.3 and the ablation studies",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        508.6463623046875,
        503.9974365234375,
        517.5529174804688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "on sampling strategies in Appendix B.4.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        519.5553588867188,
        268.07904052734375,
        528.4619140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Nie et al. [27] suggests that MDM requires 16 times more computation than ARM to achieve the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        535.9443359375,
        503.9991149902344,
        544.8508911132812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "same likelihood. However, key differences make our findings more broadly applicable. In particular,",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        546.8533935546875,
        505.2428283691406,
        555.7599487304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "likelihood is a relatively indirect metric for downstream task performance, and diffusion optimizes a",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        557.7623291015625,
        503.9977722167969,
        566.6688842773438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "bound of the likelihood, making it not directly comparable to ARM. Additionally, we extended the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        568.67138671875,
        503.99859619140625,
        577.5779418945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "scaling range from 1018 ∼1020 FLOPs in Nie et al. [27] to 1020 ∼1023 FLOPs in this work.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        575.248046875,
        480.0979919433594,
        588.4869384765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3.2",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        609.1968383789062,
        120.4532470703125,
        618.1531982421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Benchmark Results",
      "bbox": [
        130.4158477783203,
        609.1968383789062,
        213.71315002441406,
        618.1531982421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To comprehensively evaluate the in-context learning and instruction-following capabilities of LLaDA",
      "bbox": [
        107.69100189208984,
        631.40234375,
        504.3605041503906,
        640.3088989257812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "8B, we conducted detailed comparisons with existing LLMs [6, 21, 25, 26, 32, 33] of similar scale.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        642.3113403320312,
        505.7435302734375,
        651.2178955078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Task selection and evaluation protocols followed existing studies, covering popular benchmarks in",
      "bbox": [
        107.69100189208984,
        653.2203369140625,
        503.9980773925781,
        662.1268920898438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "general tasks, mathematics, code, and Chinese. Further details are provided in Appendix B.6. For a",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        664.12939453125,
        503.99725341796875,
        673.0359497070312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "more direct comparison, we re-evaluated representative LLMs [6, 21] in our implementation.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        675.038330078125,
        478.4094543457031,
        683.9448852539062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "As shown in Tab. 1, after pretraining on 2.3T tokens, LLaDA 8B Base demonstrates remarkable",
      "bbox": [
        107.64099884033203,
        691.4273681640625,
        504.0042724609375,
        700.3339233398438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "performance, surpassing LLaMA2 7B Base on nearly all tasks, and is overall competitive with",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        702.3363647460938,
        503.9971618652344,
        711.242919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "LLaMA3 8B Base. LLaDA shows advantages in math and Chinese tasks. We conjecture that the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        713.245361328125,
        503.9974670410156,
        722.1519165039062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "6",
      "bbox": [
        303.5090026855469,
        743.1333618164062,
        308.49029541015625,
        752.0399169921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    }
